          "source": "palm",
          "analysis": "The binary is a statically-linked Linux backdoor/RAT. It establishes persistence by creating init.d scripts and cron jobs (e.g., `/etc/init.d/%s`, `/etc/cron.hourly/%s.sh`). It performs command and control (C2) communication using HTTP GET/POST requests with spoofed User-Agent strings (e.g., `Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; ...)`). The malware gathers extensive system information by reading from the `/proc` filesystem, including network connections (`/proc/net/tcp`), process information (`/proc/%d/exe`), and system details (`/proc/cpuinfo`, `/proc/sys/kernel/version`). It also reads a configuration file from `/etc/daemon.cfg`.",
